  "body": "The compiled counter, controlled form, keyed list and deterministic effect now run through both React and a standalone DOM renderer. One existing runtime and one actual GoScript module remain authoritative across synchronous renderer replacement; state, cached Go View, focus/selection and pending effects survive without additional Init/Update/View calls or application dispatches. No handwritten JavaScript application reducer or WASM is introduced.\n\nStacks on PR #11, exact parent `184ccdaabe9e6e46e1052ee79cd7e0be26fe3281`. Published head `832d21262ce5dd3bd1d308a19bd8d7a422f6d7cb`, tree `bc8883df935c7d0c8b7265831cacdf5521fb70d2`; local checkpoint `89eb373c7f87119cacf5254a70f405d61c529e96` has the same tree and parent. PR1 already covers the interactive-counter milestone; this advances the next composed replaceability boundary.\n\n### Executed locally\n\n- Five fixtures, 43 logical application ticks across React-only, DOM-only and alternating profiles; 37 swaps, 9 focused swaps, 45 detected mutation controls, zero mismatches. Independent reviews verify exact state/tree/bindings, mounted DOM/live properties, ordering, pending effects and callback lifetime classification.\n- Both actual backend builds: four apps, 209 outputs each, 204 byte-identical companion files. Separate raw bundle hashes are retained; one concrete module per app is used across renderers.\n- Current compiler regression: 33 commands, 97/97 Node tests, Go tests/race/vet, 43 matched ticks and 89 mutation controls, zero mismatches.\n- Full inherited chain: 5,000 static cases, seed20261030, 59 executable rules; all24 original SHA receipts intact. Typed composition: 63 scripts, 2,463 actions/native frames, 4,926 actor comparisons, zero mismatches; seeds20261030/20261031.\n- Real HTTP demo: five passing checks on four cards. Standalone DOM counter boot: seven bundle inputs, no React packages/adapters/externals, no WASM/fetch/XHR.\n- Local Go1.24.0/compiler Go1.27.3, Node22.23.4, React19.3.1, Chromium153.0.8010.0. Local inherited/compiler/backend commands were separate passing executions; a fresh uninterrupted default CI run is pending.\n\n### Inspect and reproduce\n\n[Commands, versions, seeds, failures, tested/untested scope](https://github.com/samuelpmahan/gondola/blob/832d21262ce5dd3bd1d308a19bd8d7a422f6d7cb/compiled-backends/RESULTS.md) · [Demo and build instructions](https://github.com/samuelpmahan/gondola/blob/832d21262ce5dd3bd1d308a19bd8d7a422f6d7cb/compiled-backends/README.md) · [Renderer contract](https://github.com/samuelpmahan/gondola/blob/832d21262ce5dd3bd1d308a19bd8d7a422f6d7cb/compiled-backends/CONTRACT.md).\n\n`bash run-compiled-backends.sh` runs inherited gates then the compiler/backend matrix and HTTP smoke. `--backends-only` is explicitly partial. After building, serve the repository and open `compiled-backends/artifacts/demo/`.\n\nThe verified retained archive contains all2,019 files in both current artifact directories, 356,910,490 uncompressed bytes; archive SHA-256 `734887fcdf2d31f1aa75fc2e0ffc4b45b308ded0e585423ab02fcbee557ef1f7`, 9,577,956 bytes. Its member index, generated code, native executables, browser traces, screenshots, historical failed attempts and exact execution receipts are inspectable in the branch.\n\nSix actual Luna6 XHigh workers used unmodified native Rebalancer1.0.4 from toolkit PR1 head989c295, with disjoint ownership, dependency gates and independent review. All26 packets and15 native epochs close with capacity/eligibility checks, equal native/exact scores and zero broken constraints. Actual platform deliveries are recorded separately from native allocation. Historical metadata mistakes and amended reviews are retained and recursively resolved.\n\nThis is finite serialized synchronous Chromium evidence, not universal Go/frontend equivalence. Actual retained native DOM listener execution, other engines, hydration, IME, pixels, concurrent React, production transport and committed-state rollback remain untested. The next composed milestone is compiling existing typed parent/child and session ownership contracts through both renderers with subtree cancellation.\n\nNo main merge or production deployment. Draft while fresh published-source CI executes.",
